From d861200492af93d89b59410736a1c1025f1e28fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omalawn <omalawn@local>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:31:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] omalawn silent update: install itself without a tap (Android
 12+)

Once "Install unknown apps" is allowed, the checked update is written into
a PackageInstaller session of this app's own package (MODE_FULL_INSTALL,
setAppPackageName, USER_ACTION_NOT_REQUIRED) and committed right after the
link's answer went out, since a silent install replaces this process; the
link comes back on MY_PACKAGE_REPLACED as before. The last chunk's answer
carries silent: true when Android's rule lets it through without the user
(an installer updating itself, UPDATE_PACKAGES_WITHOUT_USER_ACTION, which
is now declared, and the APK's targetSdk at least 29/30/31/33 on Android
12/13/14/15). UpdateResultReceiver takes the outcome: on
STATUS_PENDING_USER_ACTION the update notification comes up and its tap
opens Android's confirmation for that session; on a failure the
notification says why and its tap opens the installer the old way.
A session Android has not answered at all after 45 s (no status, not even
pending user action) is abandoned and gets that notification too: Google Play Protect can hold a silent install of a build
it does not know with no screen to ask on (seen on the AVD). Android also
allows one silent update per package and installer every 30 s, so a
second one sooner needs the tap.
The update notification's tap intent is made afresh each time
(FLAG_CANCEL_CURRENT): with FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT a live record kept its old
flags, so a tap could bring back a left-behind settings page instead of
the installer or the confirmation.
The receiver logs each outcome (installed, pending_user_action, failed)
with the predicted silent flag, and PREDICTION_MISMATCH when a predicted
silent install asked for the user. A session prepared for an offer that
then fails is abandoned at once, so no later chunk can commit it.
Without "Install unknown apps", or before Android 12, the notification is
as before. Debug hook debug_update_require_user_action makes sessions ask
for the user, to drive the fallback on a device; debug_update_reset also
abandons this app's sessions.
